    {
      "id": "FEAT-013",
      "name": "Driver Behaviour Analysis",
      "status": "implemented",
      "description": "Multi-source driving behaviour monitoring: GPS positions feed the gps-position-worker (speed violations, idle-excess detection). ESP32 accelerometer events feed the behaviour-event-consumer via MQTT (harsh braking, harsh acceleration, sudden swerve). AI camera events also arrive via the same MQTT consumer (see FEAT-014). All events are persisted to driving_events. On trip completion a BullMQ job scores the trip across 5 dimensions (speed, driving style, fatigue, idle, SOS) using configurable weights and thresholds stored in behaviour_scoring_config. Completed behaviour_reports are viewable per trip and in a fleet-wide safety ranking on the admin behaviour dashboard. Thresholds and score weights are editable by admins.",
